    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "But here's the catch, leaving the dollar is much harder than talking about it. To replace it, a currency needs huge open markets, money that can move freely across borders, and courts that investors trust. China still tightly controls money moving in and out of the country. The euro has no single government standing behind it. Most of the world's trade deals, loans and savings are still written in dollars, and unwinding all of that would take decades. So for now, the world keeps running on dollars, not because everyone loves the dollar, but because nothing else is ready.",
